Validation failed for tool "submit_decision":
  - answers: must have required properties answers

Received arguments:
{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "severity": "urgent",
  "summary": "The emailed request to move Margaret Ellison's (L-02) rent income to a new account is treated as suspected payment fraud: the sender domain differs from the CRM, the Reply-To is a Protonmail address, and the email uses urgency and says she cannot take calls. No bank details were changed. The 12 Oct payout of £1,932 stays on the account ending 9902 pending call-back verification and dual approval, and fraud has been escalated (ESC-102).</summary>\n<parameter name=\"answers\">[{\"question\":\"Should the bank details be changed?\",\"answer\":\"No. Not on this email. Changes need a phone call-back to the number already on file (+447700900202) and dual staff approval. The sender domain (ellisonletings.co.uk) differs from the CRM (ellisonlettings.co.uk), the Reply-To is a Protonmail address, and the request pushes urgency and refuses calls. The only genuine signal (22 Sep email) came from the CRM domain.\"},{\"question\":\"What happens to the payout scheduled for Monday?\",\"answer\":\"No hold was needed because no payee change was applied. The £1,932 payout on 12 Oct 09:00 stays on the existing account ending 9902. If call-back verification fails or is not completed by Monday morning, the payout should be held for fraud review (escalated to fraud, ESC-102).\"},{\"question\":\"Who do you contact and through which channel?\",\"answer\":\"Margaret Ellison by phone call-back on the number on file (+447700900202), which I could not action with my tools, so fraud must complete it. I emailed her on the CRM address (MSG-103) to say no change has been made and that we will verify by phone. The escalation goes to the fraud team.\"}]",
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Internal note NOTE-101 on L-02 recording the fraud risk and that no bank change was made."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Fraud escalation ESC-102 (P2) with the handover packet, deadline 12 Oct 08:30."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Email MSG-103 to margaret@ellisonlettings.co.uk (CRM address) saying no change has been made and that we will verify by phone."
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1 (attempt 1)",
      "handling": "send_message returned HTTP 500 and was not applied. Retried once to the CRM address and it verified as MSG-103."
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    "Sender domain in the email (ellisonletings.co.uk) differs from the CRM and previous email (ellisonlettings.co.uk). Trusted the CRM and the previous genuine email.",
    "Email asks for a change, but the CRM and payout schedule still show account ending 9902. Trusted the system record, since the request is unverified."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The phone call-back has not been completed. I have no phone tool, so fraud must do it on +447700900202 before Monday.",
    "The CRM payout record (9902) is current."
  ]
}

